# CoW 2G — mutation in a MATCH SCRUTINEE inside a loop body. `match xs.pop():`
# evaluates the scrutinee every iteration; the prescan's Match arm previously
# scanned only the arm bodies, missing the scrutinee. With the 2G scrutinee scan
# the loop-carried materialize fires and the pops persist across iterations.
#
# In known_gaps/ (out of the runtime-diff corpus) pending the self-host CoW-2G
# mirror closing the same scrutinee hole. Rust lane is correct.
void f(Vector[int] xs):
    int i = 0
    while i < 3:
        match xs.pop():
            case Some(v):
                print(v)
            case None:
                print(0 - 1)
        i = i + 1
    print(xs.len())

void main():
    Vector[int] a = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
    f(a)
    print(a.len())
